 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "kiddushin.76b.5",
   "daf": "76b",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "וְלֹא מִסַּנְהֶדְרִין וּלְמַעְלָה. מַאי טַעְמָא? דְּתָנֵי רַב יוֹסֵף: כְּשֵׁם שֶׁבֵּית דִּין מְנוּקִּין בְּצֶדֶק – כָּךְ מְנוּקִּין מִכׇּל מוּם. אָמַר מָרִימָר: מַאי קְרָאָה – ״כֻּלָּךְ יָפָה רַעְיָתִי וּמוּם אֵין בָּךְ״.",
   "en": "The mishna also taught: «Nor» must one investigate «from the Sanhedrin and above. What is the reason» there is no need to investigate further? The Gemara answers: It is «as Rav Yosef taught» that «just as the court is clean in justice, so too, it is clean of any blemish,» i.e., it does not include anyone of flawed lineage. «Mareimar said: What is the verse» from which it is derived? It states: «“You are all fair, my love; and there is no blemish in you”» (Song of Songs 4:7)."
  }
 ],
